From: Radical <radical@radical.fun>
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dbus): support touch values in SendEvent

CompositeDevice.SendEvent's array handling only builds Vector2/Vector3, so
external callers have no way to drive a Touchpad(*::Touch::Motion)
capability: the touchpad target's motion handler pattern-matches on
InputValue::Touch specifically (index, is_touching, pressure, x, y) and
silently no-ops on anything else, including a Vector2 of just (x, y).

Accept a 5-element array of [index, is_touching, x, y, pressure] and build
an InputValue::Touch from it, alongside the existing 2/3-element cases.
---
 src/dbus/interface/composite_device.rs | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/dbus/interface/composite_device.rs b/src/dbus/interface/composite_device.rs
index e3db7ac..dd6db39 100644
--- a/src/dbus/interface/composite_device.rs
+++ b/src/dbus/interface/composite_device.rs
@@ -273,6 +273,28 @@ impl CompositeDeviceInterface {
                         z: Some(z),
                     }
                 }
+                // [index, is_touching, x, y, pressure]. Used for touchpad/touchscreen
+                // motion capabilities, whose native value carries a multi-touch slot
+                // and touch state alongside position, unlike a plain Vector2.
+                5 => {
+                    let mut parts = [0f64; 5];
+                    for (i, part) in parts.iter_mut().enumerate() {
+                        let item: &Value = v.get(i).unwrap().unwrap();
+                        *part = f64::try_from(item).map_err(|_| {
+                            fdo::Error::Failed(
+                                "Failed to parse touch value into float.".to_string(),
+                            )
+                        })?;
+                    }
+                    let [index, is_touching, x, y, pressure] = parts;
+                    InputValue::Touch {
+                        index: index as u8,
+                        is_touching: is_touching != 0.0,
+                        pressure: Some(pressure),
+                        x: Some(x),
+                        y: Some(y),
+                    }
+                }
                 _ => InputValue::None,
             },
             _ => InputValue::None,
